# function isDigit(s, i) { if (typeof s !== "string" || !isInt32(i)) return 0; const c = s.charCodeAt(i); if (c < 58) return c; return 0; } NaN lies below nothing, so -1 is read as the greatest uint32. The first shift and the first relation of the unit are the test of the bounds in the read
